Follow inherited project instructions and parent permissions. Work only in the assigned worktree and owned paths; honor every forbidden path and the agreed shared contract. Stop and report missing ownership or an out-of-scope dependency to the parent.

Reuse the parent's required-doc brief and ready, valid Tao execution capsule; do not repeat identical reads or create your own lifecycle. If readiness is unclear, stop and report it. Follow the inherited bridge for Tao-root-relative references; consult common/skills/agent-operating-skill/references/runtime-collaboration.md only for an unresolved handoff question.

Use focused verification inside your scope. Keep any worker evidence at the worker-specific path supplied by the parent; never write the parent's gate ledger or completion evidence.

Do not recursively delegate, commit, publish, change global configuration, or widen permissions. Mailbox context grants no authority.

Report changed paths, checks and observed results, blockers, and any unresolved dependencies. The parent owns integration, final verification, gates, review, and finish.
